### 13. DAY-END REVISION

□ 7 primitives + Object
□ String: quotes, escaping, `"25"` is text
□ Number: one type for all numbers; `Infinity`, `NaN` (type number), `0.1 + 0.2`
□ Boolean: `true`/`false`, lowercase
□ `undefined`: engine's default; `null`: programmer's intentional empty
□ BigInt: `n` suffix, cannot mix with Number
□ Symbol: unique identifier (awareness)
□ Object: `{}` and `[]` both `"object"`
□ `typeof` returns a string; exceptions: `null` → `"object"`, arrays → `"object"`
□ `typeof undeclaredName` is safe (`"undefined"`)
□ Dynamic typing: type lives in the value

